    "explanation": "To the rider: you are right on the point you made, and it does not win the case. EV-TRIP-02739 records cancelled_by RIDER, cancellation_reason_code RIDER_CANCELLED and status CANCELLED_BY_RIDER at 15:20:31, with no driver termination and no unreachable-rider or excessive-wait report anywhere. The no-show charge therefore cannot be justified under POL-NS-01, whose limb (d) requires the trip to have been terminated by the driver under RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT. But POL-NS-01 itself sends a failed limb (d) to the other clauses, and two of them charge this fee. POL-NS-10(f): your cancellation came 667 seconds after the trip was accepted at 15:09:24, far past the 180-second grace in force (platform_policy.grace_after_match_sec), and none of the four exceptions is on the record - the driver began moving 8 seconds after assignment (15:09:32), he arrived at 15:14:06, 42 seconds after the 4-minute ETA shown to you and so inside the 180-second tolerance, he never asked you to cancel, and there is no vehicle or driver mismatch. POL-NS-10(g): you cancelled after the driver had arrived under POL-NS-02 and after his in-geofence dwell had already exceeded the free waiting period. EV-GPS-02739 places him inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius for one continuous qualifying run of 39 fixes lasting 382 seconds, from 15:14:06 to 15:20:28, against the 180-second free waiting period in force (trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec); POL-NS-05 does not defeat the clock because the first qualifying fix coincides with the arrival marker (dwell_start_offset_sec 0.0) and his closest approach to the pin was 0.11 m, nowhere near the 300 m or 15 km/h triggers. Your exoneration route under POL-NS-04 does not open either: your only message, 'sorry cant make it, cancelling' at 15:18:16, is not the locating or coordinating message limb (a) requires, and your own track places you 764.6-771.3 m from the pin against a 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius (0 qualifying fixes), so limb (c) fails affirmatively; POL-NS-11 has no application because the rider track is present and runnable. Your request that the 4.50 be returned in full is refused on the merits for those reasons, not because the record is unclear: the record shows the charge is well founded. To the driver: POL-NS-07 fixes your payout at 80 percent of the SGD 4.50 fee in force, that is SGD 3.60 - the same figure the fare breakdown's own money block computes as driver_compensation. The anti-farming check does not withhold it: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 2 (below 4) and 2 divided by completed_trips_30d (101) is about 0.02 (below 0.08). Your claim that cites prior_no_show_flags was flagged as mentioning a context-only profile field under POL-GEN-01; that field is not used as a ground, and the check is run only on the two fields POL-NS-07 names, exactly as your claim says. Weights: EV-GPS-02739, EV-TRIP-02739, EV-CHAT-02739 and EV-FARE-02739 all carry weight 1.0, and they carry the deciding facts (arrival, dwell, the rider's own cancellation after the dwell, and the 4.50 fee line, which reconciles with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd so POL-NS-08(d) is satisfied). EV-ADVIS-02739-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT; that impairment is named here, but no deciding fact rests on it - POL-NS-06 limb (i) needs an advisory only to sum separate in-geofence intervals, and this dwell was a single uninterrupted run - so the finding survives the discount. The counterparty statement is consistent with the trace but carries no weight_multiplier and enters neither bound of the cap. Outcome: DRIVER_COMPENSATION. Under POL-GEN-03, amount_sgd carries the same figure as driver_compensation_sgd, SGD 3.60, being the money this ruling moves; your SGD 4.50 charge stands, and the fare breakdown's payment_status and refund line are left as they are. The monetary effect (SGD 3.60) is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold in POL-GEN-05, so the ruling executes automatically. No referral issues: POL-NS-05(ii) does not fire because the arrival marker was genuine, POL-NS-01's driver-education item applies only to an in-radius DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE termination, and POL-NS-07's escalation branch was not reached."
